    mahjong_kw("mahjong-quads.html", "Quads Hands", "Quads in mahjong — four-of-a-kind hands on the NMJL card.", "quads mahjong, mah jongg quads hand", "Quads in Mahjong", "<p><strong>Quads</strong> hands require four of a kind — a common category on the NMJL card. Learn to read them: <a href=\"read-nmjl-card.html\">Read the card</a> · <a href=\"mahjong-102.html\">102</a>.</p>"),
    mahjong_kw("second-right-pass-mahjong.html", "Second Right Pass", "Second right pass in the Charleston — passing tiles to the right.", "second right pass mahjong, charleston pass right mah jongg", "Second Right Pass in the Charleston", "<p>Round two of the Charleston — <strong>pass to the right</strong>. Full sequence in <a href=\"mahjong-101.html\">Mahjong 101</a> · <a href=\"first-left-pass-mahjong.html\">First left pass</a>.</p>"),
    mahjong_kw("across-pass-mahjong.html", "Across Pass", "Across pass in the Charleston — passing tiles across the table.", "across pass mahjong, charleston pass across mah jongg", "Across Pass in the Charleston", "<p>Round three — <strong>pass across</strong> the table to your opposite player. Learn the full Charleston: <a href=\"mahjong-charleston.html\">Charleston guide</a>.</p>"),
    mahjong_kw("mahjong-wall.html", "The Wall", "The mahjong wall — building and breaking the tile wall.", "mahjong wall, mah jongg wall tiles", "The Mahjong Wall", "<p>Players build a <strong>wall</strong> of face-down tiles — then break it to deal. Learn dealing in <a href=\"mahjong-101.html\">Mahjong 101</a> · <a href=\"east-seat-mahjong.html\">East seat</a>.</p>"),
    mahjong_kw("break-wall-mahjong.html", "Break the Wall", "Breaking the wall in mahjong — how dealing starts.", "break wall mahjong, mah jongg break wall deal", "Break the Wall", "<p>The dealer <strong>breaks the wall</strong> with dice to start dealing. Full process taught in <a href=\"mahjong-101.html\">Mahjong 101</a> · <a href=\"mahjong-dice.html\">Dice</a>.</p>"),
    mahjong_kw("redeem-joker-mahjong.html", "Redeem a Joker", "Redeem a joker in mahjong — swapping a natural tile for a joker.", "redeem joker mahjong, mah jongg joker exchange", "Redeem a Joker", "<p>You can <strong>redeem a joker</strong> by swapping the matching natural tile from your hand. Joker rules in <a href=\"mahjong-jokers.html\">Jokers guide</a> · <a href=\"mahjong-101.html\">101</a>.</p>"),
    mahjong_kw("like-numbers-mahjong.html", "Like Numbers Hands", "Like numbers in mahjong — matching number hands on the NMJL card.", "like numbers mahjong, mah jongg like numbers hand", "Like Numbers in Mahjong", "<p><strong>Like numbers</strong> hands use matching digits across suits — a popular NMJL category. <a href=\"read-nmjl-card.html\">Read the card</a> · <a href=\"mahjong-hands.html\">Hands</a>.</p>"),
    mahjong_kw("year-hand-mahjong.html", "Year Hands", "Year hands in mahjong — annual year-category on the NMJL card.", "year hand mahjong, mah jongg year category", "Year Hands in Mahjong", "<p><strong>Year hands</strong> on the NMJL card use the digits of the current year — a fan favorite category. <a href=\"mahjong-card-2026.html\">2026 card</a> · <a href=\"read-nmjl-card.html\">Read the card</a>.</p>"),
    mahjong_kw("mahjong-runs.html", "Runs & Consecutives", "Runs in mahjong — consecutive tile sequences on the NMJL card.", "runs mahjong, consecutive mah jongg hand", "Runs in Mahjong", "<p><strong>Runs</strong> and consecutives are core NMJL hand patterns — three or more tiles in sequence. <a href=\"mahjong-hands.html\">Hands</a> · <a href=\"mahjong-102.html\">102</a>.</p>"),
    mahjong_kw("charleston-courtesy-mahjong.html", "Courtesy Pass", "Courtesy pass in the Charleston — optional fourth pass in American mah jongg.", "courtesy pass mahjong, charleston courtesy mah jongg", "Courtesy Pass in the Charleston", "<p>After three rounds, players may agree to a <strong>courtesy pass</strong> — an optional fourth exchange. Taught in <a href=\"mahjong-101.html\">Mahjong 101</a> · <a href=\"optional-pass-mahjong.html\">Optional pass</a>.</p>"),
